# Used with: scripts/e2e.sh tests/e2e/select-autoscroll.actions -- target/debug/temzdf standalone pdf --clean target/fixtures/sample-short.pdf
# Coordinates assume the default 900x600 window (fit width, page 1 at the top).
# Judged: dragging from the title into the bottom edge and holding scrolls
# the document by itself while the selection grows, until the end of the
# two pages (held, expect: the bottom of page 2; the autoscroll there takes
# under 2 s, held 4 s, so the screen no longer depends on how many frames
# the viewer drew); releasing copies the selection, from the title to the
# document's last line (clipboard.txt; copied and to-end, check).
# held judges where the view stopped, not where the selection ends: no
# selected text is in view there (the pointer stays left of the page
# number, which WezTerm's pixel to the right selected), and the replay's
# selection stays on page 1 (page 2's text is not loaded while it runs
# through the autoscroll; todo.md); to-end judges the real selection's end.
pause 1
down 318 188
# kitty on macOS reports a press followed at once by motion at the motion's
# position (the selection then started below the title).
sleep 0.1
for y in 260 360 460 560 575; do move 300 $y; sleep 0.05; done
# To the end (under 2 s) and a margin.
pause 4
expect held
up
pause 0.5
clipboard >"$outdir/clipboard.txt" || true
check copied grep -q "^temzdf sample document" "$outdir/clipboard.txt"
check to-end sh -c 'tail -n 1 "$1" | grep -qx "The end, with a last needle."' sh "$outdir/clipboard.txt"
